1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:02,320
Luke. Luke 1.

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:09,440
Inasmuch as many have undertaken to compile a narrative of the things that have been accomplished among us,

3
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:15,400
just as those who from the beginning were eyewitnesses and ministers of the Word have delivered them to us,

4
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:21,060
it seemed good to me also, having followed all things closely for some time past,

5
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,860
to write an orderly account for you, most excellent Theophilus,

6
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:28,780
that you may have certainty concerning the things you have been taught.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,980
In the days of Herod, king of Judea, there was a priest named Zechariah, of the division of Abijah,

8
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:40,200
and he had a wife from the daughters of Aaron, and her name was Elizabeth.

9
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:47,400
And they were both righteous before God, walking blamelessly in all the commandments and statutes of the Lord.

10
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:53,580
But they had no child, because Elizabeth was barren, and both were advanced in years.

11
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:58,680
Now while he was serving as priest before God when his division was on duty,

12
00:00:59,260 --> 00:00:59,980
according to the custom,

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,020
he was chosen by lot to enter the temple of the Lord and burn incense.

14
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:10,360
And the whole multitude of the people were praying outside at the hour of incense.

15
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:16,640
And there appeared to him an angel of the Lord, standing on the right side of the altar of incense.

16
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:21,620
And Zechariah was troubled when he saw him, and fear fell upon him.

17
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:23,560
But the angel said to him,

18
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:28,780
Do not be afraid, Zechariah, for your prayer has been heard,

19
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:34,120
and your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son, and you shall call his name John.

20
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:39,160
And you will have joy and gladness, and many will rejoice at his birth,

21
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:41,780
for he will be great before the Lord.

22
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:47,940
And he must not drink wine or strong drink, and he will be filled with the Holy Spirit,

23
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,680
even from his mother's womb.

24
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:54,680
And he will turn many of the children of Israel to the Lord their God,

25
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:58,580
and he will go before him in the spirit and power of Elijah.

26
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,520
To turn the hearts of the fathers to the children,

27
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:04,640
and the disobedient to the wisdom of the just,

28
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:07,940
to make ready for the Lord a people prepared.

29
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:10,880
And Zechariah said to the angel,

30
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:18,120
How shall I know this? For I am an old man, and my wife is advanced in years.

31
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:20,540
And the angel answered him,

32
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:25,020
I am Gabriel. I stand in the presence of God,

33
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,400
and I was sent to speak to you,

34
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:28,740
and to bring you this gospel,

35
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:29,400
good news.

36
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:34,020
And behold, you will be silent and unable to speak

37
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:36,360
until the day that these things take place,

38
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,700
because you did not believe my words,

39
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:41,480
which will be fulfilled in their time.

40
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,880
And the people were waiting for Zechariah,

41
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:47,860
and they were wondering at his delay in the temple.

42
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:51,440
And when he came out, he was unable to speak to them,

43
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:54,960
and they realized that he had seen a vision in the temple,

44
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:58,640
and he kept making signs to them and remained mute.

45
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:02,200
And when his time of service was ended, he went to his home.

46
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:05,400
After these days his wife Elizabeth conceived,

47
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:08,580
and for five months she kept herself hidden, saying,

48
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:13,160
Thus the Lord has done for me in the days when he looked on me,

49
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:16,240
to take away my reproach among people.

50
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:20,540
In the sixth month the angel Gabriel was sent from God

51
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:22,720
to a city of Galilee named Nazareth,

52
00:03:22,860 --> 00:03:27,160
to a virgin betrothed to a man whose name was Joseph of the house of David.

53
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:29,480
And the virgin's name was Mary.

54
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:31,720
And he came to her and said,

55
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:38,520
But she was greatly troubled at the saying,

56
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:41,580
and tried to discern what sort of greeting this might be.

57
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:43,640
And the angel said to her,

58
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:48,640
Do not be afraid, Mary, for you have found favor with God.

59
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:53,580
And behold, you will conceive in your womb and bear a son,

60
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:56,500
and you shall call his name Jesus.

61
00:03:57,160 --> 00:04:01,140
He will be great, and will be called the Son of the Most High.

62
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:05,760
And the Lord God will give to him the throne of his father David,

63
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:09,140
and he will reign over the house of Jacob forever,

64
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:12,560
and of his kingdom there will be no end.

65
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:14,960
And Mary said to the angel,

66
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:18,500
How will this be, since I am a virgin?

67
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,840
And the angel answered her,

68
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:23,580
The Holy Spirit will come upon you,

69
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:26,800
and the power of the Most High will overshadow you.

70
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:31,000
Therefore, the child to be born will be called Holy,

71
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:32,720
the Son of God.

72
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:37,660
And behold, your relative Elizabeth in her old age

73
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:39,360
has also conceived a son.

74
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:44,960
And this is the sixth month with her who was called barren,

75
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:48,360
for nothing will be impossible with God.

76
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:50,440
And Mary said,

77
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:53,860
Behold, I am the servant of the Lord.

78
00:04:54,340 --> 00:04:56,560
Let it be to me according to your word.

79
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:58,940
And the angel departed from her.

80
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:04,560
In those days Mary arose and went with haste into the hill country to a town in Judah.

81
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:08,340
And she entered the house of Zechariah and greeted Elizabeth.

82
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:11,280
And when Elizabeth heard the greeting of Mary,

83
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:13,320
the baby leaped in her womb,

84
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:16,400
and Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit,

85
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:19,180
and she exclaimed with a loud cry,

86
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:22,000
Blessed are you among women,

87
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,780
and blessed is the fruit of your womb.

88
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:27,140
And why is this granted to me?

89
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:29,580
That the mother of my Lord should come to me?

90
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:34,160
For behold, when the sound of your greeting came to my ears,

91
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:36,860
the baby in my womb leaped for joy.

92
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:41,200
And blessed is she who believed that there would be a fulfillment

93
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,920
of what was spoken to her from the Lord.

94
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:45,760
And Mary said,

95
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:48,600
My soul magnifies the Lord,

96
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:51,460
and my spirit rejoices in God my Savior,

97
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:54,540
for he has looked on the humble estate of his servant.

98
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:57,040
For behold, from now on,

99
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:59,360
all generations will call me blessed.

100
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,280
For he who is mighty has done great things for me,

101
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:05,060
and holy is his name,

102
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:08,260
and his mercy is for those who fear him

103
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:10,400
from generation to generation.

104
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:13,540
He has shown strength with his arm,

105
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:16,340
he has scattered the proud in the thoughts of their hearts.

106
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:19,300
He has brought down the mighty from their thrones,

107
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:21,720
and exalted those of humble estate.

108
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:24,760
He has filled the hungry with good things,

109
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:26,760
and the rich he has sent away empty.

110
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:31,960
He has helped his servant Israel in remembrance of his mercy,

111
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:37,660
as he spoke to our fathers, to Abraham, and to his offspring forever.

112
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:41,960
And Mary remained with her about three months and returned to her home.

113
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:47,960
Now the time came for Elizabeth to give birth, and she bore a son.

114
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:53,060
And her neighbors and relatives heard that the Lord had shown great mercy to her,

115
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:55,060
and they rejoiced with her.

116
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:57,060
And on the eighth day,

117
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,060
they came to circumcise the child.

118
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,560
And they would have called him Zechariah after his father.

119
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:04,060
But his mother answered,

120
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:08,060
No, he shall be called John.

121
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,560
And they said to her,

122
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:13,060
None of your relatives is called by this name.

123
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:17,560
And they made signs to his father inquiring what he wanted him to be called.

124
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:20,860
And he asked for a writing tablet and wrote,

125
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:22,560
His name is John.

126
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:24,560
And they all wondered.

127
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:26,960
And immediately his mouth was opened,

128
00:07:27,460 --> 00:07:28,460
and his tongue loosed,

129
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:29,460
and he spoke,

130
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:30,460
blessing God.

131
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,960
And fear came on all their neighbors.

132
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:36,460
And all these things were talked about through all the hill country of Judea.

133
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:39,960
And all who heard them laid them up in their hearts, saying,

134
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,960
What then will this child be?

135
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:45,460
For the hand of the Lord was with him,

136
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:48,960
and his father Zechariah was filled with the Holy Spirit,

137
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:50,460
and prophesied, saying,

138
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:53,960
Blessed be the Lord God of Israel,

139
00:07:54,460 --> 00:07:56,460
for he has visited and redeemed his people.

140
00:07:57,460 --> 00:08:02,960
And has raised up a horn of salvation for us in the house of his servant David.

141
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:07,460
As he spoke by the mouth of his holy prophets from of old,

142
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:12,460
that we should be saved from our enemies and from the hand of all who hate us,

143
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:17,960
to show the mercy promised to our fathers and to remember his holy covenant,

144
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:21,960
the oath that he swore to our father Abraham,

145
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:26,460
to grant us that we, being delivered from the hand of our enemies,

146
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:29,460
might serve him without fear,

147
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:34,460
in holiness and righteousness before him all our days.

148
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:37,460
And you, child,

149
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:40,460
will be called the prophet of the Most High,

150
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:44,460
for you will go before the Lord to prepare his ways,

151
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:49,960
to give knowledge of salvation to his people in the forgiveness of their sins,

152
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:52,960
because of the tender mercy of our God,

153
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:55,960
whereby the sunrise shall visit us from on high,

154
00:08:56,960 --> 00:09:01,460
to give light to those who sit in darkness and in the shadow of death,

155
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:05,460
to guide our feet into the way of peace.

156
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:08,960
And the child grew and became strong in spirit,

157
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:13,460
and he was in the wilderness until the day of his public appearance to Israel.

